    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6c2772b9-6c4c-5d48-afe2-aa21b5f82f89",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=6-x,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (3,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (1,5)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-1$ and $y$-intercept $6,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/1d590c557317df0b07aef98ec5a0b249d39ebbc357d5b958ec4e0fb600ce3a72-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ it is also invertible on $x\\in (3,\\infty)$ and $x\\in (1,5).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
