      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=3x+3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (9,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in [-6,4)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $3$ and $y$-intercept $3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/73bf1ce66aed14ce487f3bf8d5a86448d73d067c46e48895e00f82ccec60fc5e-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (9,\\infty)$ and $x\\in [-6,4).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
