  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124474,
      "id": "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d",
      "title": "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2b3c0506-7b1b-5c20-9627-81ad4d9e5237",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=4x+3,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (8,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in [-7,3)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $4$ and $y$-intercept $3,$ as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/616ee00abb06f77af0dc7bbb5abc479f4cae5ad4bbcb8a366d7dfc12a25d491b-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ it is also invertible on  $x\\in (8,\\infty)$ and $x\\in [-7,3).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bde8e079-df71-5873-85c8-a9ae88a8b2fe",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
