    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0b83c5c7-5e85-577e-834a-91343804adcd",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)=4-3x,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-4,\\infty)$\n- **III.** $x\\in (-6,-2)$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The function $f(x)$ is a linear function with slope $-3$ and $y$-intercept $4,$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124474/plots/774bfa6de19dc59aba94b9da61d6572d935c9e3e0541813784f8d7d890a08d2e-0.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- The given function is invertible on the interval $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ On this interval, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n- Since the function is invertible on $x\\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ it is also invertible on $x\\in (-4,\\infty)$ and $x\\in (-6,-2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
